.TH SDL_SetJoystickPlayerIndex 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_SetJoystickPlayerIndex \- Set the player index of an opened joystick.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_joystick.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_SetJoystickPlayerIndex(SDL_Joystick *joystick, int player_index);
.fi
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I joystick
the
.BR SDL_Joystick
obtained from
.BR SDL_OpenJoystick ()\[char46]

.TP
.I player_index
player index to assign to this joystick, or -1 to clear the player index and turn off player LEDs\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetJoystickPlayerIndex (3)
